{title: Ring the Bells of Heaven}
{artist: William O. Cushing / George F. Root}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Opening}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Broadman Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: Broadman Press, 1940), # 124)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Ring the bells of Heaven! There is [D]joy today,
[E7]For a soul, returning from the [A]wild!
[A]See, the Father meets him out up[D]on the way,
[E7]Welcoming His weary, wandering [A]child.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Glory! [E7]Glory! How the [F#m]angels [C#]sing:
[D]Glory! [B]Glory! How the [E]loud [B7]harps [E]ring!
[A]’Tis the ransomed army, like a [D]mighty sea,
[E7]Pealing forth the anthem of the [A]free.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Ring the bells of Heaven! There is [D]joy today,
[E7]For the wanderer now is recon[A]ciled;
[A]Yes, a soul is rescued from his [D]sinful way,
[E7]And is born anew a ransomed [A]child.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Ring the bells of Heaven! Spread the [D]feast today!
[E7]Angels, swell the glad triumphant [A]strain!
[A]Tell the joyful tidings, bear it [D]far away!
[E7]For a precious soul is born a[A]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
